From ac58a3258455e2485def5d936530e641f8168690 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:07:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(import): flip the flat cap facets of a refined STEP
 face

The #2600 split holds a curved face's facet edges to its surface. It
measures edges only, so it left flat "cap" facets on the wall of
bar_cross_holes.step: three points on the cylinder, the apex over the
middle of the long edge. Their normals stood up to 65 degrees off the
radius (2 147 of 131 834 wall facets over 25 degrees). The feature graph
read their edges as creases on the smooth wall: 3 701 pickable edges, and
116 tangent pieces that feature_edge_g1_join refused. Main was red.

A refined face now gets Lawson's edge flip, measured in space: an inside
edge whose two opposite angles sum to more than a half turn becomes the
other diagonal, when the new facets keep their winding in the parameter
plane and the new edge passes the split's chord-height limit. No point
moves and no boundary edge changes. The worst wall normal is 6.5 degrees
off; the bar has 642 pickable edges and 0 split pieces.

Pinned by feature_edge_g1_join:
no_pickable_edge_is_a_tangent_piece_of_a_longer_one_in_any_step_fixture
and tilted_gouge: the_step_bars_wall_facet_normals_follow_the_cylinder.

Fixes #2713

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
